From cfe64292bfd23d187b5a9409e712098e28b259d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Voice Bot <voicebot@local>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 20:14:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] r4 exit footsteps: live steps on the character's real foot
 plants (room wood/rug, door slab, path/grass), no baked steps in the exit
 track

Funning on 09a1b8e: no footsteps while she walks in the home room; after the door, sudden sharp loud steps.
Cause: the only steps were baked into sfx_exit_outbound (8b22546/A1). That track starts at 'crossing-out', on a
fixed 0.56 s grid. The steps set its normalisation peak (about 0 to 5 dB under BGM+wind+waves, peak -3 dBFS).

- FootstepData.ts (generated by tools/exit-footsteps/derive_footsteps.cjs, --check in tests):
  - per-clip foot-plant times plus the sole contact point, from the shipped character GLB (FK at 480 Hz; sole <= 4 mm after a >= 10 mm lift);
  - a 0.1 m surface map of the shipped room/island GLB (ground_map_blender.py): W wood, R rug, S stone slab, P sand path, G grass.
- FootstepCore.ts: engine-free tracker. It observes the stand-in motion clock (read-only; standin, CharacterMotion and
  anim_meta stay frozen) and fires the crossed plants with a 25 ms lead. It also has the surface lookup at the planted
  sole, and a variant picker (no immediate repeat, +-1.5 dB).
- FootstepAudio.ts: created by WorldIntegrationBoot (outside the frozen section), fed the world states, ticked in Boot.lateUpdate.
  It loads region_island/audio_steps and plays through GameAudio.play, so mute, sfx mute and background drop steps without queueing.
- GameAudio: step names in SfxName, plus adoptClips()/hasClip(). It does not import the footstep modules.
- assets: 20 synthesised mono mp3s (27.5 KB, LPF 4.5 kHz), with metas.
- exit track: regenerated without the baked steps (same size; whoosh + air bed only).
- test exit-footsteps (17 cases, run-suite):
  - real flow sim at 30/45/60(+jitter)/120 fps, exit + return: 52/52 plants with one step each, |err| <= 40 ms, 0 extra, 0 wrong surfaces;
  - mute / sfx mute / background / state gating with mock Cocos;
  - assets.
